diff --git a/Documentation/criu.txt b/Documentation/criu.txt
index 19ecf3e01..e5b8f04c8 100644
--- a/Documentation/criu.txt
+++ b/Documentation/criu.txt
@@ -453,6 +453,14 @@ mount -t cgroup -o devices,freezer none devices,freezer
     The option only engages for plain, uncompressed images without a parent
     image chain; other images fall back to the usual path.
 
+*--premap-hugepage*::
+    Together with *--premap-threads*, align every premapped private memory
+    area of 2 MiB or more to a 2 MiB boundary that keeps the phase of its
+    final address, and advise *MADV_HUGEPAGE* on it, so the kernel backs it
+    with transparent huge pages while it is populated and keeps them through
+    the final move into place. This raises the speed at which a device driver
+    or the task itself can later read the memory back.
+
 *--timeout* 'number'::
     Set a time limit in seconds for collecting tasks during the
     dump operation. The timeout is 10 seconds by default.
